{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And showing lovingkindness</b> — four times in the Masorah. Two in the Decalogue. And two concerning David: ועשה חסד למשיחו לו — one who shows lovingkindness to others, lovingkindness is shown to him. And David practiced lovingkindness even to non-Jews, as written: ויאמר דוד אעשה חסד עם חנון. Therefore lovingkindness was shown to him." "<b>And those who keep My commandments</b> — and adjacent to it: לא תשא. This teaches that the severity of an oath in vain is like all the commandments. Another interpretation: to teach that when you keep the commandments, be careful not to do them in vain — not for their own sake; rather do them for their own sake. On the shin of לא תשא there are seven crowns, corresponding to the seven times כזב appears in Ezekiel; seven abominations in his heart; seven sin-offerings in the rebuke; ז' עונותיכם מלאים; seven names of the evil inclination; seven rungs of Gehinnom."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:44.796986020Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}